.css-68drzi{text-align:center;font-family:var(--font-montserrat);font-weight:600;font-size:1.5rem;line-height:2rem;margin:0 0 25px;} Nepal rescuers pull a Chinese national and a woman alive 10 days after devastating floods

Updated: 6:33 AM CDT Sep 5, 2026 Editorial Standards ⓘ

.css-ncbpmr{padding-left:0;margin-top:18px;margin-right:3px;float:left;font-weight:700;font-size:1.125rem;line-height:1.7;font-family:var(--font-source-sans-pro);}@media only screen and (min-width: 41.25rem){.css-ncbpmr{margin-left:60px;margin-top:0px;}}

Rescuers in Nepal pulled out a Chinese man and a woman in separate operations Saturday, 10 days after devastating floods hit the country, as teams continued searching for thousands of people still missing.

The man was rescued from a hydropower tunnel, according to a social media post by the country’s prime minister’s office, bringing the total to three workers pulled alive from the Trishuli hydropower project. Two Nepalese workers were rescued on Friday.

