.css-1fsc1be{text-align:center;position:-webkit-sticky;position:sticky;top:.9375rem;width:100%;height:auto;margin-bottom:.9375rem;}@media only screen and (min-width: 41.25rem){.css-1fsc1be{width:100%;min-height:250px;height:auto;overflow:hidden;}} .css-19es0j2{min-height:250px;height:auto;}.css-19es0j2 img{margin:0 auto;} Advertisement

Nepal's army said a joint rescue team of Nepalese military personnel and South Korean disaster experts rescued the man from a 225-meter tunnel (about 738 feet) and that he was undergoing a health assessment. Images showed him being evacuated by helicopter, with an army medic checking on him during the flight.

